# Every text file is checked out with LF, on every platform.
#
# This is not a style preference. `docs/api-index.json` and
# `docs/developer-index.json` are generated by reading documentation strings
# out of the source, so a working tree carrying CRLF produces indexes that
# differ from the committed ones and `cargo run -p xtask -- api check` fails —
# on Windows, for reasons that have nothing to do with the change under test.
# The Windows validation runner had to restore files from their Git blobs by
# hand to get a gate to pass, more than once, before this line existed.
#
# Every text blob in this repository is already LF, so this pins what is
# already true rather than renormalising anything.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The visual baselines are compared byte for byte by the headless gate, and
# the bundled faces, captures and archives are not text at all. `text=auto`
# would detect these as binary anyway; saying so explicitly means a future
# format never has to rely on that detection being right.
*.png binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.mov binary
*.gltf binary
*.tar binary

# A patch is bytes that have to apply, so nothing may touch its endings.
*.patch -text

# The frozen historical import receipt. It predates the rule above and is
# named separately so it stays exact whatever that rule becomes.
vendor/block/src/lib.rs text eol=lf
